-- # Class: OcsfLdapPerson Description: The additional LDAP attributes that describe a person.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: cost_center Description: The cost center associated with the user.
--     * Slot: created_time Description: The timestamp when the user was created.
--     * Slot: created_time_dt Description: The timestamp when the user was created.
--     * Slot: deleted_time Description: The timestamp when the user was deleted. In Active Directory (AD), when a user is deleted they are moved to a temporary container and then removed after 30 days. So, this field can be populated even after a user is deleted for the next 30 days.
--     * Slot: deleted_time_dt Description: The timestamp when the user was deleted. In Active Directory (AD), when a user is deleted they are moved to a temporary container and then removed after 30 days. So, this field can be populated even after a user is deleted for the next 30 days.
--     * Slot: department Description: The name of the department in which the user works.
--     * Slot: display_name Description: The display name of the LDAP person. According to RFC 2798, this is the preferred name of a person to be used when displaying entries.
--     * Slot: employee_uid Description: The employee identifier assigned to the user by the organization.
--     * Slot: given_name Description: The given or first name of the user.
--     * Slot: hire_time Description: The timestamp when the user was or will be hired by the organization.
--     * Slot: hire_time_dt Description: The timestamp when the user was or will be hired by the organization.
--     * Slot: job_title Description: The user's job title.
--     * Slot: last_login_time Description: The last time when the user logged in.
--     * Slot: last_login_time_dt Description: The last time when the user logged in.
--     * Slot: ldap_cn Description: The LDAP and X.500 <code>commonName</code> attribute, typically the full name of the person. For example, <code>John Doe</code>.
--     * Slot: ldap_dn Description: The X.500 Distinguished Name (DN) is a structured string that uniquely identifies an entry, such as a user, in an X.500 directory service For example, <code>cn=John Doe,ou=People,dc=example,dc=com</code>.
--     * Slot: leave_time Description: The timestamp when the user left or will be leaving the organization.
--     * Slot: leave_time_dt Description: The timestamp when the user left or will be leaving the organization.
--     * Slot: modified_time Description: The timestamp when the user entry was last modified.
--     * Slot: modified_time_dt Description: The timestamp when the user entry was last modified.
--     * Slot: office_location Description: The primary office location associated with the user. This could be any string and isn't a specific address. For example, <code>South East Virtual</code>.
--     * Slot: phone_number Description: The telephone number of the user. Corresponds to the LDAP <code>Telephone-Number</code> CN.
--     * Slot: surname Description: The last or family name for the user.
--     * Slot: location_id Description: The geographical location associated with a user. This is typically the user's usual work location.
--     * Slot: manager_id Description: The user's manager. This helps in understanding an org hierarchy. This should only ever be populated once in an event. I.e. there should not be a manager's manager in an event.
-- # Class: OcsfLoadBalancer Description: The load balancer object describes the load balancer entity and contains additional information regarding the distribution of traffic across a network.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: classification Description: The request classification as defined by the load balancer.
--     * Slot: code Description: The numeric response status code detailing the connection from the load balancer to the destination target.
--     * Slot: error_message Description: The load balancer error message.
--     * Slot: ip Description: The IP address of the load balancer node that handled the client request. Note: the load balancer may have other IP addresses, and this is not an IP address of the target/distribution endpoint - see <code>dst_endpoint</code>.
--     * Slot: message Description: The load balancer message.
--     * Slot: status_detail Description: The status detail contains additional status information about the load balancer distribution event.
--     * Slot: name Description: The name of the load balancer.
--     * Slot: uid Description: The unique identifier for the load balancer.
--     * Slot: uid_numeric Description: The <code>uid</code> attribute in numeric form where applicable.<br><strong>Note:</strong> Producers may populate <code>uid_numeric</code> only in addition to <code>uid</code> and not as an alternative to it.
--     * Slot: dst_endpoint_id Description: The destination to which the load balancer is distributing traffic.
-- # Class: OcsfLocation Description: The Geo Location object describes a geographical location, usually associated with an IP address.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: aerial_height Description: Expressed as either height above takeoff location or height above ground level (AGL) for a UAS current location. This value is provided in meters and must have a minimum resolution of 1 m. Special Values: <code>Invalid</code>, <code>No Value</code>, or <code>Unknown: -1000 m</code>.
--     * Slot: city Description: The name of the city.
--     * Slot: continent Description: The name of the continent.
--     * Slot: country Description: The ISO 3166-1 Alpha-2 country code.<p><b>Note:</b> The two letter country code should be capitalized. For example: <code>US</code> or <code>CA</code>.</p>
--     * Slot: desc Description: The description of the geographical location.
--     * Slot: geodetic_altitude Description: The aircraft distance above or below the ellipsoid as measured along a line that passes through the aircraft and is normal to the surface of the WGS-84 ellipsoid. This value is provided in meters and must have a minimum resolution of 1 m. Special Values: <code>Invalid</code>, <code>No Value</code>, or <code>Unknown: -1000 m</code>.
--     * Slot: geodetic_vertical_accuracy Description: Provides quality/containment on geodetic altitude. This is based on ADS-B Geodetic Vertical Accuracy (GVA). Measured in meters.
--     * Slot: geohash Description: <p>Geohash of the geo-coordinates (latitude and longitude).</p>Geohashing is a geocoding system used to encode geographic coordinates in decimal degrees, to a single string.
--     * Slot: horizontal_accuracy Description: Provides quality/containment on horizontal position. This is based on ADS-B NACp. Measured in meters.
--     * Slot: is_on_premises Description: Indicates whether the location is on-premises.
--     * Slot: isp Description: The name of the Internet Service Provider (ISP).
--     * Slot: lat Description: The geographical Latitude coordinate represented in Decimal Degrees (DD). For example: <code>42.361145</code>.
--     * Slot: long Description: The geographical Longitude coordinate represented in Decimal Degrees (DD). For example: <code>-71.057083</code>.
--     * Slot: postal_code Description: The postal code of the location.
--     * Slot: pressure_altitude Description: The uncorrected barometric pressure altitude (based on reference standard 29.92 inHg, 1013.25 mb) provides a reference for algorithms that utilize 'altitude deltas' between aircraft. This value is provided in meters and must have a minimum resolution of 1 m.. Special Values: <code>Invalid</code>, <code>No Value</code>, or <code>Unknown: -1000 m</code>.
--     * Slot: provider Description: The provider of the geographical location data.
--     * Slot: region Description: The alphanumeric code that identifies the principal subdivision (e.g. province or state) of the country. For example, 'CH-VD' for the Canton of Vaud, Switzerland
--     * Slot: OcsfUnmannedSystemOperatingArea_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
-- # Class: OcsfLogger Description: The Logger object represents the device and product where events are stored with times for receipt and transmission.  This may be at the source device where the event occurred, a remote scanning device, intermediate hops, or the ultimate destination.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: event_uid Description: The unique identifier of the event assigned by the logger.
--     * Slot: is_truncated Description: Indicates whether the OCSF event data has been truncated due to size limitations. When <code>true</code>, some event data may have been omitted to fit within system constraints.
--     * Slot: log_format Description: The format of data in the log. For example JSON, syslog or CSV.
--     * Slot: log_level Description: The level at which an event was logged. This can be log provider specific. For example the audit level.
--     * Slot: log_name Description: The log name for the logging provider log, or the file name of the system log. This may be an intermediate store-and-forward log or a vendor destination log. For example /archive/server1/var/log/messages.0 or /var/log/.
--     * Slot: log_provider Description: The logging provider or logging service that logged the event. This may be an intermediate application store-and-forward log or a vendor destination log.
--     * Slot: log_version Description: The event log schema version of the original event. For example the syslog version or the Cisco Log Schema version
--     * Slot: logged_time Description: The time when this logger received and logged the event. For the last logger in the pipeline, this value should match <code>metadata.logged_time</code>.
--     * Slot: logged_time_dt Description: The time when this logger received and logged the event. For the last logger in the pipeline, this value should match <code>metadata.logged_time</code>.
--     * Slot: transmit_time Description: The time when the event was transmitted from the logging device to it's next destination.
--     * Slot: transmit_time_dt Description: The time when the event was transmitted from the logging device to it's next destination.
--     * Slot: untruncated_size Description: The original size of the OCSF event data in kilobytes before any truncation occurred. This field is typically populated when <code>is_truncated</code> is <code>true</code> to indicate the full size of the original event.
--     * Slot: version Description: The version of the logging provider.
--     * Slot: name Description: The name of the logging product instance.
--     * Slot: uid Description: The unique identifier of the logging product instance.
--     * Slot: uid_numeric Description: The <code>uid</code> attribute in numeric form where applicable.<br><strong>Note:</strong> Producers may populate <code>uid_numeric</code> only in addition to <code>uid</code> and not as an alternative to it.
--     * Slot: OcsfMetadata_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: device_id Description: The device where the events are logged.
--     * Slot: product_id Description: The product logging the event.  This may be the event source product, a management server product, a scanning product, a SIEM, etc.
-- # Class: OcsfLongString Description: This object is a used to capture strings which may be truncated by a security product due to their length.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: is_truncated Description: Indicates that <code>value</code> has been truncated. May be omitted if truncation has not occurred.
--     * Slot: untruncated_size Description: The size in bytes of the string represented by <code>value</code> before truncation. Should be omitted if truncation has not occurred.
--     * Slot: value Description: The string value, truncated if <code>is_truncated</code> is <code>true</code>.
-- # Class: OcsfMalware Description: The Malware object describes the classification of known malicious software, which is intentionally designed to cause damage to a computer, server, client, or computer network.
