-- # Class: OcsfNetworkTraffic Description: The Network Traffic object describes characteristics of network traffic over a time period. The metrics represent network data transferred between source and destination during an observation window.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: bytes Description: The total number of bytes transferred in both directions (sum of bytes_in and bytes_out).
--     * Slot: bytes_in Description: The number of bytes sent from the destination to the source (inbound direction).
--     * Slot: bytes_missed Description: The number of bytes that were missed during observation, typically due to packet loss or sampling limitations.
--     * Slot: bytes_out Description: The number of bytes sent from the source to the destination (outbound direction).
--     * Slot: chunks Description: The total number of chunks transferred in both directions (sum of chunks_in and chunks_out).
--     * Slot: chunks_in Description: The number of chunks sent from the destination to the source (inbound direction).
--     * Slot: chunks_out Description: The number of chunks sent from the source to the destination (outbound direction).
--     * Slot: end_time Description: The end time of the observation or reporting period.
--     * Slot: end_time_dt Description: The end time of the observation or reporting period.
--     * Slot: packets Description: The total number of packets transferred in both directions (sum of packets_in and packets_out).
--     * Slot: packets_in Description: The number of packets sent from the destination to the source (inbound direction).
--     * Slot: packets_out Description: The number of packets sent from the source to the destination (outbound direction).
--     * Slot: start_time Description: The start time of the observation or reporting period.
--     * Slot: start_time_dt Description: The start time of the observation or reporting period.
--     * Slot: timespan_id Description: The time span object representing the duration of the observation or reporting period.
-- # Class: OcsfNode Description: Represents a node or a vertex in a graph structure.
--     * Slot: id
