--     * Slot: OcsfAnomaly_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: OcsfBaseline_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: timespan_id Description: The time window when the value or event was first observed. It is used to analyze activity patterns, detect trends, or correlate events within a specific timeframe.
-- # Class: OcsfOccurrenceDetails Description: Details about where in the target entity, specified information was discovered. Only the attributes, relevant to the target entity type should be populated.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: cell_name Description: The cell name/reference in a spreadsheet. e.g <code>A2</code>
--     * Slot: column_name Description: The column name in a spreadsheet, where the information was discovered.
--     * Slot: column_number Description: The column number in a spreadsheet or a plain text document, where the information was discovered.
--     * Slot: end_line Description: The line number of the last line of the file, where the information was discovered.
--     * Slot: json_path Description: The JSON path of the attribute in a json record, where the information was discovered
--     * Slot: page_number Description: The page number in a document, where the information was discovered.
--     * Slot: record_index_in_array Description: The index of the record in the array of records, where the information was discovered. e.g. the index of a record in an array of JSON records in a file.
--     * Slot: row_number Description: The row number in a spreadsheet, where the information was discovered.
--     * Slot: start_line Description: The line number of the first line of the file, where the information was discovered.
--     * Slot: OcsfDiscoveryDetails_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
-- # Class: OcsfOrganization Description: The Organization object describes characteristics of an organization or company and its division if any. Additionally, it also describes cloud and Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) logical hierarchies such as AWS Organizations, Google Cloud Organizations, Oracle Cloud Tenancies, and similar constructs.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: ou_name Description: The name of an organizational unit, Google Cloud Folder, or AWS Org Unit. For example, the <code> GCP Project Name </code>, or <code> Dev_Prod_OU </code>.
--     * Slot: ou_uid Description: The unique identifier of an organizational unit, Google Cloud Folder, or AWS Org Unit. For example, an  <code> Oracle Cloud Tenancy ID </code>, <code> AWS OU ID </code>, or <code> GCP Folder ID </code>.
--     * Slot: name Description: The name of the organization, Oracle Cloud Tenancy, Google Cloud Organization, or AWS Organization. For example, <code> Widget, Inc. </code> or the <code> AWS Organization name </code>.
--     * Slot: uid Description: The unique identifier of the organization, Oracle Cloud Tenancy, Google Cloud Organization, or AWS Organization. For example, an <code> AWS Org ID </code> or <code> Oracle Cloud Domain ID </code>.
--     * Slot: uid_numeric Description: The <code>uid</code> attribute in numeric form where applicable.<br><strong>Note:</strong> Producers may populate <code>uid_numeric</code> only in addition to <code>uid</code> and not as an alternative to it.
-- # Class: OcsfOs Description: The Operating System (OS) object describes characteristics of an OS, such as Linux or Windows.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: build Description: The operating system build number.
--     * Slot: country Description: The operating system country code, as defined by the ISO 3166-1 standard (Alpha-2 code).<p><b>Note:</b> The two letter country code should be capitalized. For example: <code>US</code> or <code>CA</code>.</p>
--     * Slot: cpe_name Description: The Common Platform Enumeration (CPE) name. For example: <code>cpe:/a:apple:safari:16.2</code>.
--     * Slot: cpu_bits Description: The cpu architecture, the number of bits used for addressing in memory. For example: <code>32</code> or <code>64</code>.
--     * Slot: edition Description: The operating system edition. For example: <code>Professional</code>.
--     * Slot: kernel_release Description: The kernel release of the operating system. On Unix-based systems, this is determined from the <code>uname -r</code> command output, for example "5.15.0-122-generic".
--     * Slot: lang Description: The two letter lower case language codes, as defined by ISO 639-1. For example: <code>en</code> (English), <code>de</code> (German), or <code>fr</code> (French).
--     * Slot: name Description: The operating system name.
--     * Slot: sp_name Description: The name of the latest Service Pack.
--     * Slot: sp_ver Description: The version number of the latest Service Pack.
--     * Slot: type Description: The type of the operating system.
--     * Slot: type_id Description: The type identifier of the operating system.
--     * Slot: version Description: The version of the OS running on the device that originated the event. For example: "Windows 10", "OS X 10.7", or "iOS 9".
-- # Class: OcsfOsint Description: The OSINT (Open Source Intelligence) object contains details related to an indicator such as the indicator itself, related indicators, geolocation, registrar information, subdomains, analyst commentary, and other contextual information. This information can be used to further enrich a detection or finding by providing decisioning support to other analysts and engineers.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: category Description: Categorizes the threat indicator based on its functional or operational role.
--     * Slot: comment Description: Analyst commentary or source commentary about an indicator or OSINT analysis.
--     * Slot: confidence Description: The confidence of an indicator or analysis, normalized to the caption of the confidence_id value. In the case of 'Other', it is defined by the event source or analyst.
--     * Slot: confidence_id Description: The normalized identifier of the confidence level, reflecting the accuracy or pertinence of the OSINT indicator or analysis. A low confidence indicates that the collected information lacked sufficient detail or accuracy to fully qualify the indicator as malicious. When the value is <code>99</code> (Other), the <code>confidence</code> attribute must contain the source-specific label.
--     * Slot: created_time Description: The timestamp when the indicator was initially created or identified.
--     * Slot: created_time_dt Description: The timestamp when the indicator was initially created or identified.
--     * Slot: desc Description: A detailed explanation of the indicator, including its context, purpose, and relevance.
--     * Slot: detection_pattern Description: The specific detection pattern or signature associated with the indicator.
--     * Slot: detection_pattern_type Description: The detection pattern type, normalized to the caption of the detection_pattern_type_id value. In the case of 'Other', it is defined by the event source.
--     * Slot: detection_pattern_type_id Description: Specifies the type of detection pattern used to identify the associated threat indicator.
--     * Slot: expiration_time Description: The expiration date of the indicator, after which it is no longer considered reliable.
--     * Slot: expiration_time_dt Description: The expiration date of the indicator, after which it is no longer considered reliable.
--     * Slot: external_uid Description: A unique identifier assigned by an external system for cross-referencing.
--     * Slot: modified_time Description: The timestamp of the last modification or update to the indicator.
--     * Slot: modified_time_dt Description: The timestamp of the last modification or update to the indicator.
--     * Slot: name Description: The <code>name</code> is a pointer/reference to an attribute within the OCSF event data. For example: file.name.
--     * Slot: risk_score Description: A numerical representation of the threat indicator’s risk level.
--     * Slot: severity Description: Represents the severity level of the threat indicator, typically reflecting its potential impact or damage.
--     * Slot: severity_id Description: The normalized severity level of the threat indicator, typically reflecting its potential impact or damage.
--     * Slot: src_url Description: The source URL of an indicator or OSINT analysis, e.g., a URL back to a TIP, report, or otherwise.
--     * Slot: subnet Description: A CIDR or network block related to an indicator or OSINT analysis.
--     * Slot: tlp Description: The Traffic Light Protocol (TLP) was created to facilitate greater sharing of potentially sensitive information and more effective collaboration. TLP provides a simple and intuitive schema for indicating with whom potentially sensitive information can be shared.
--     * Slot: type Description: The OSINT indicator type.
--     * Slot: type_id Description: The OSINT indicator type ID.
--     * Slot: uid Description: The unique identifier for the OSINT object.
--     * Slot: uploaded_time Description: The timestamp indicating when the associated indicator or intelligence was added to the system or repository.
--     * Slot: uploaded_time_dt Description: The timestamp indicating when the associated indicator or intelligence was added to the system or repository.
--     * Slot: value Description: The actual indicator value in scope, e.g., a SHA-256 hash hexdigest or a domain name.
--     * Slot: vendor_name Description: The vendor name of a tool which generates intelligence or provides indicators.
