-- # Class: OcsfPacket Description: The Packet object represents a single captured network packet and its associated metadata. It describes where the packet came from, how it is stored or encoded, and how it can be located within a capture file or stream. This object does not interpret protocol content; it only represents the captured packet data and its positioning information.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: encoding Description: The human-readable name of the encoding used to represent the packet data in the <code>value</code> field. This should match the caption associated with <code>encoding_id</code>. If <code>encoding_id</code> is 99 (Other), this field contains the original data source–specific encoding value.
--     * Slot: encoding_id Description: The normalized identifier of the encoding method used to represent the packet data as a string.
--     * Slot: end_offset Description: The ending byte position of this packet within a capture file or stream.
--     * Slot: format Description: The human-readable name of the packet capture file format in which the packet is stored. This should match the caption associated with <code>format_id</code>. If <code>format_id</code> is 99 (Other), this field contains the original data source–specific format value.
--     * Slot: format_id Description: The normalized identifier of the packet capture format.
--     * Slot: sequence_number Description: The relative order number of this packet within its capture context (such as a PCAP file, network session, or reconstructed stream). This represents chronological capture order, distinct from both protocol-level sequencing (such as TCP sequence numbers).
--     * Slot: source Description: The human-readable name describing how or where the packet was obtained. This should match the caption associated with <code>source_id</code>. If <code>source_id</code> is 99 (Other), this field contains the original data source–specific value.
--     * Slot: source_id Description: A normalized numeric identifier that specifies how the packet was obtained or generated.
--     * Slot: start_offset Description: The starting byte position of this packet within a capture file or stream.
--     * Slot: value Description: The actual packet data, represented as a string. The format of this string is determined by the specified <code>encoding_id</code> (e.g., Base64, Hexadecimal, or URL Encoded).
--     * Slot: OcsfNetworkEvent_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: OcsfDhcpActivity_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: OcsfDnsActivity_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
