--     * Slot: references Description: Provides a reference to an external source of information related to the CTI being represented. This may include a URL, a document, or some other type of reference that provides additional context or information about the CTI.
-- # Class: OcsfOsint_subdomains
--     * Slot: OcsfOsint_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: subdomains Description: Any pertinent subdomain information - such as those generated by a Domain Generation Algorithm - related to an indicator or OSINT analysis.
-- # Class: OcsfPeripheralDevice_vendor_id_list
--     * Slot: OcsfPeripheralDevice_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: vendor_id_list Description: The list of vendor IDs for the peripheral device.
-- # Class: OcsfPermissionAnalysisResult_granted_privileges
--     * Slot: OcsfPermissionAnalysisResult_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: granted_privileges Description: The specific privileges, actions, or permissions that are explicitly granted by the analyzed policy. Examples: AWS actions like <code>s3:GetObject</code>, <code>ec2:RunInstances</code>, <code>iam:CreateUser</code>; Azure actions like <code>Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/read</code>; or GCP permissions like <code>storage.objects.get</code>.
-- # Class: OcsfProcess_lineage
--     * Slot: OcsfProcess_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: lineage Description: The lineage of the process, represented by a list of paths for each ancestor process. For example: <code>['/usr/sbin/sshd', '/usr/bin/bash', '/usr/bin/whoami']</code>.
-- # Class: OcsfProcess_loaded_modules
--     * Slot: OcsfProcess_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: loaded_modules Description: The list of loaded module names.
-- # Class: OcsfRemediation_kb_articles
--     * Slot: OcsfRemediation_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: kb_articles Description: The KB article/s related to the entity. A KB Article contains metadata that describes the patch or an update.
-- # Class: OcsfRemediation_references
--     * Slot: OcsfRemediation_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: references Description: A list of supporting URL/s, references that help describe the remediation strategy.
-- # Class: OcsfRequest_flags
--     * Slot: OcsfRequest_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: flags Description: The communication flags that are associated with the api request.
-- # Class: OcsfResourceDetails_labels
--     * Slot: OcsfResourceDetails_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: labels Description: The list of labels associated to the resource.
-- # Class: OcsfResponse_flags
--     * Slot: OcsfResponse_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: flags Description: The communication flags that are associated with the api response.
-- # Class: OcsfService_labels
--     * Slot: OcsfService_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: labels Description: The list of labels associated with the service.
-- # Class: OcsfSso_scopes
--     * Slot: OcsfSso_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: scopes Description: Scopes define the specific permissions or actions that the client is allowed to perform on behalf of the user. Each scope represents a different set of permissions, and the user can selectively grant or deny access to specific scopes during the authorization process.
-- # Class: OcsfStartupItem_run_mode_ids
--     * Slot: OcsfStartupItem_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: run_mode_ids Description: The list of normalized identifiers that describe the startup items' properties when it is running.  Use this field to capture extended information about the process, which may depend on the type of startup item.  E.g., A Windows service that interacts with the desktop.
-- # Class: OcsfStartupItem_run_modes
--     * Slot: OcsfStartupItem_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: run_modes Description: The list of run_modes, normalized to the captions of the run_mode_id values.  In the case of 'Other', they are defined by the event source.
-- # Class: OcsfTicket_status_details
--     * Slot: OcsfTicket_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: status_details Description: A list of contextual descriptions of the <code>status, status_id</code> values.
-- # Class: OcsfTls_certificate_chain
--     * Slot: OcsfTls_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: certificate_chain Description: The Chain of Certificate Serial Numbers field provides a chain of Certificate Issuer Serial Numbers leading to the Root Certificate Issuer.
-- # Class: OcsfTls_client_ciphers
--     * Slot: OcsfTls_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: client_ciphers Description: The client cipher suites that were exchanged during the TLS handshake negotiation.
-- # Class: OcsfTls_server_ciphers
--     * Slot: OcsfTls_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: server_ciphers Description: The server cipher suites that were exchanged during the TLS handshake negotiation.
-- # Class: OcsfTrace_flags
--     * Slot: OcsfTrace_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: flags Description: The flags associated with the trace, used to indicate specific properties or behaviors, such as whether the trace is sampled or if it has special handling. Flags help control how traces are processed, logged, and analyzed, providing valuable context for tracing and observability tools in identifying trace characteristics or specific tracking requirements.
-- # Class: OcsfTrait_values
--     * Slot: OcsfTrait_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: values Description: The values of the trait.
-- # Class: OcsfUnmannedSystemOperatingArea_coordinates
--     * Slot: OcsfUnmannedSystemOperatingArea_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: coordinates Description: A two-element array, containing a longitude/latitude pair. The format conforms with GeoJSON. For example: <code>[-73.983, 40.719]</code>.
-- # Class: OcsfUrl_categories
--     * Slot: OcsfUrl_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: categories Description: The Website categorization names, as defined by <code>category_ids</code> enum values.
-- # Class: OcsfUrl_category_ids
--     * Slot: OcsfUrl_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: category_ids Description: The Website categorization identifiers.
-- # Class: OcsfVulnerability_kb_articles
--     * Slot: OcsfVulnerability_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: kb_articles Description: The KB article/s related to the entity. A KB Article contains metadata that describes the patch or an update.
